 "brief": "A wrist link that joins two servos with perpendicular axes, MJF PA12. Servo A's horn is at the\norigin with its axis along Z: the link bolts to it with a 20 mm diameter, 3 mm thick disc\n(z = 0 to 3) and four M2 screws on a 14 mm circle (at (7,0), (-7,0), (0,7), (0,-7)). Servo B's\nhorn is 60 mm away along X with its axis along Y: a 20 mm diameter, 3 mm thick disc at x = 60,\nz = 20, from y = 12 to 15, with four M2 screws on a 14 mm circle in that disc's plane. Servo B's\nbody (x = 45 to 75, y = -12 to 12, z = 5 to 35) must stay clear. The part fits in x = -12 to 72,\ny = -12 to 15, z = 0 to 34. Servo A holds it. The gripper beyond servo B is 1 kg on a moving arm\nwith its centre of mass 100 mm further out along +X, and servo B can stall at 2 N\u00b7m about Y.\nSafety factor 2.",
